  "program": {
    "module": {
      "summary": "Housing Act 1988 s.21 — validity of a notice seeking possession of an\nassured shorthold tenancy (post-Deregulation Act 2015 regime).\n\nTop-level output is a statutory conclusion (`section_21_notice_valid`\n: holds / not_holds / undetermined) rather than a monetary amount. No\narithmetic on the question asked — only a cascade of legal judgments,\nabsence conditions, and named time windows composed from several Acts:\n\n  HA 1988 s.19A + Sch 2A          tenancy must be an AST\n  HA 2004 s.213(3)                deposit protected within 30 days\n  HA 2004 s.213(6)                prescribed information within 30 days\n  HA 2004 s.215                   s.21 barred if scheme duties unmet\n  DerA 2015 s.38 + SI 2015/1646   EPC / gas safety / How-to-Rent guide\n  HA 2004 Parts 2/3 + DerA s.41   licensing duty\n  DerA 2015 s.33                  retaliatory-eviction bar\n  HA 1988 s.21(4B)                no notice in the first four months\n\nThe retaliation bar is expressed with the `count_where` filtered-\naggregation extension: each CouncilNotice carries an input\n`is_in_retaliation_window: Boolean` pre-computed by the caller (the\nserved-on date falls 0–180 days before the s.21 notice was served)."
    },
